1 Purpose and weekly focus
During Week 6, I focused on preparing the ShieldSense interface and accessibility evidence for the progress presentation. My work supported the team’s held-out evaluation by checking how classifier outcomes were communicated to users, reviewing the Green, Amber and Red risk presentation, and identifying interface improvements needed before the formal accessibility pass and feature freeze in Week 7.
2 Work completed
Risk result interface review
I reviewed the way low-, medium- and high-risk results appear in the web interface. I checked that each result includes a clear risk label, a short plain-language explanation and an appropriate next-step message. This approach reduces reliance on technical terminology and helps users understand why a message may be suspicious.
Accessibility and usability checks
I carried out an initial accessibility review against the main WCAG 2.2 AA requirements relevant to the prototype. I checked that colour was supported by visible text labels, interactive controls could be identified clearly, headings and instructions were understandable, and the layout remained readable at different screen sizes. I recorded issues to be addressed during the Week 7 accessibility pass.
Support for evaluation and error analysis
I examined how held-out test examples were displayed after classification, with particular attention to cases where the predicted category could be unclear to a user. I noted that the interface must present the model output consistently and must not overstate certainty. Where a result is Amber or Red, the screen should provide practical guidance such as avoiding links, verifying the sender independently and not sharing personal information.
Progress presentation preparation
I prepared and rehearsed the section of the progress presentation covering the interface design, risk-colour system, accessibility decisions and my individual contribution. I used supervisor feedback to make the explanation more focused on visible evidence, user needs and the relationship between the model result and the final warning shown on screen.
