5 Challenges and decisions required
The main challenge was presenting model output in a way that is understandable without suggesting that the classifier is always correct. The interface therefore needs consistent confidence language and clear safety advice. A client decision is required on the final wording and thresholds used for Green, Amber and Red results so that the interface matches the agreed evaluation protocol.
6 Reflection
Week 6 showed me that an accurate model alone is not enough for a responsible scam-screening application. Users must be able to understand the result, recognise the level of risk without depending only on colour and know what action to take next. Rehearsing the presentation also helped me explain my contribution more professionally by connecting each design decision to user safety and accessibility rather than describing only the visual appearance of the page.
